		plain: "Dummy variables turn a name into 0/1 columns. Keeping every level together with the intercept is a trap, because the columns add up to the intercept column.",
		situation: "There are three channels, GDN, Facebook and TikTok. Three 0/1 columns plus an intercept leave one column redundant: knowing two tells you the third. You drop one channel as the baseline. A decision tree can keep all three.",
