		prior: "The naive forecast remembers one week. A moving average remembers several weeks, and remembers them equally.",
		see: "This picture shows the simple moving average. Three bars are shaded with equal share, and the curve reacts slowly at turns.",
		plain: "A moving average adds the last few periods and divides. It smooths the series, but is slow at turns.",
		situation: "The last three weeks have 20, 24 and 80 forms. The 3-week average is (20 + 24 + 80) / 3 ≈ 41.3. The holiday week of 80 is weighed like an ordinary week. After the holiday has passed, 80 stays in the window for a while, so the forecast reacts slowly.",
