		precise: "New level = α × this week + (1 − α) × old level, with 0 < α < 1. Plugging in: 0.4 × 50 + 0.6 × 40 = 20 + 24 = 44. The forecast for every step ahead is the current level, a flat line. There is no slope component, so a trend is forecast as a standing level. Common mix-up: this α is a smoothing weight, unrelated to the α of a hypothesis test.",
		insight: "What lies ahead is a flat level, not a slope just because the past is rising.",
		symbols: []
