		precise: "Fixing rows and columns means resetting the granularity and the names. Plugging in: a table has 1,000 rows but only 940 distinct customer IDs, so 60 rows are duplicates. If each row records 500 thousand đồng, the total is inflated by 60 × 500 = 30,000 thousand đồng. Common mix-up: removing duplicates is not always right, because two real purchases are two rows. Also watch for a column that is both a name and a code, or one column holding several values, because they make GROUP BY and JOIN say the wrong thing.",
