		precise: "The Levenshtein distance is the fewest insertions, deletions and replacements. Plugging in: \"spaa\" to \"spa\" needs 1 deletion, so the distance is 1. \"massagee\" to \"massage\" is also 1. \"spa\" to \"sau\" needs 2 replacements, so the distance is 2. A phonetic hash groups words that sound alike but are spelled differently. PMI is a different tool: it is high when two words appear together more often than chance.",
		insight: "A misspelling is a number of edits. Suggest the nearest word, and don't guess on a tie.",
		symbols: ["d is the edit distance, the fewest single-character edits; in the example \"spaa\" to \"spa\" is 1."]
