		why: "So you don't train a model first and then go looking for a meeting to put it in.",
		prior: "You now have lines, probabilities, trees, clusters and word counts. None of these tools chooses the business question for you.",
		see: "This picture shows the order of steps in a business problem. Four steps light up one after another: decision, hypothesis, data, model.",
		plain: "Start from the decision and the number that would change it. The model is the last step.",
